0,Gwune language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gwune_language,"The Gwune language, also known as Agwagwune, is an Upper Cross River language of Nigeria spoken by the Akunakuna people. It is a dialect cluster named after its prestige variety; others are Abayongo, Abini, Dim, Orum, Erei, Etono.",Agwagwune,Niger-Congo
1,"Agwagwune Language, Etymology, History, Grammar, Phonology...",https://www.internationalphoneticalphabet.org/agwagwune/,"Agwagwune, also known as Agwaguna, is a language spoken by the Agwagwune people primarily in southeastern Nigeria. It belongs to the Upper Cross River subgroup of the Cross River languages, which are part of the larger Niger-Congo language family.",Agwagwune,Niger-Congo
2,Agwagwune Language (YAY) – L1 & L2 Speakers... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/yay/,Agwagwune is a stable indigenous language of Nigeria. It belongs to the Niger-Congo language family. The language is used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.,Agwagwune,Niger-Congo
